    "content": "Tax Day 2026 is Wednesday, April 15, 2026. This is the deadline for most Americans to file their 2025 federal income tax returns and pay any taxes owed. If you cannot meet this deadline, you can file IRS Form 4868 for an automatic six-month extension, shifting the filing deadline to October 15, 2026, though taxes owed must still be paid by April 15.Key details for Tax Day 2026 include:Deadline: Tax returns must be postmarked or electronically submitted by April 15, 2026.Extension: Filing an extension gives you more time to file (until Oct. 15), but not more time to pay taxes owed.Penalties: Missing the deadline without an extension can result in penalties of 5% of unpaid taxes per month, up to 25%.Exceptions: Residents of Maine and Massachusetts have until April 17, 2026, to file due to the Patriots' Day holiday, and certain military members or disaster victims may get a later deadline. Tax Day 2026 is Wednesday, April 15, 2026. This is the deadline for most Americans to file their 2025 federal income tax returns and pay any taxes owed. If you cannot meet this deadline, you can file IRS Form 4868 for an automatic six-month extension, shifting the filing deadline to October 15, 2026, though taxes owed must still be paid by April 15. IRS Form 4868 Key details for Tax Day 2026 include: Deadline: Tax returns must be postmarked or electronically submitted by April 15, 2026. Extension: Filing an extension gives you more time to file (until Oct. 15), but not more time to pay taxes owed. Penalties: Missing the deadline without an extension can result in penalties of 5% of unpaid taxes per month, up to 25%. Exceptions: Residents of Maine and Massachusetts have until April 17, 2026, to file due to the Patriots' Day holiday, and certain military members or disaster victims may get a later deadline.",
